---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, CONTACT } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Cookie Policy | ${SITE.name}`}
  description={`Which cookies ${SITE.name} sets, when, and how to change your choice.`}
>
  <section class="legal">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
      <p class="body-sm">Last updated: {new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10)}</p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        This site sets no tracking cookies. Visitor numbers are counted by Plausible, which is
        cookieless: it stores nothing on your device and reads nothing from it, so there is nothing
        there to consent to. Anything that would store something on your device stays behind the
        banner, and the consent manager is fail-closed, meaning the absence of a decision is
        treated as a refusal.
      </p>

      <h2>Categories</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Strictly necessary</strong>: a single local storage entry recording your consent
          choice so the banner does not reappear on every page. Always on; it is what makes the
          rest of this policy enforceable.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Analytics</strong>: no cookie, and nothing stored on your device. Plausible
          counts page views in aggregate, so I can see which cities people actually read about. It
          records no cross-site identifier, builds no profile, and never collects data that could
          identify you. Because it stores nothing, it runs for everyone rather than sitting behind
          the banner.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Affiliate</strong>: off by default. When enabled, affiliate attribution may set
          cookies. These are set by the partner, not by this site, and only after you click through
          to them.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Changing your mind</h2>
      <p>
        Clear this site's cookies and local storage in your browser settings and the consent banner
        returns on the next page load, letting you make a different choice.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
